API Description
The C2B API call is used as a standard customer-to-business transaction. Funds from the customer’s mobile money wallet will be deducted and be transferred to the mobile money wallet of the business. To authenticate and authorize this transaction, Mobile Money Payment Gateway will initiate a USSD Push message to the customer to gather and verify the mobile money PIN number. This number is not stored and is used only to authorize the transaction.

This API call should be utilised in combination with the "Update Transaction Status" API call. This is to allow developers the ability to first authorize a transaction’s funds and if successful, perform business functionality on the organization's side, and then later commit or uncommit the funds. If this is not done in a timely matter, the customer's funds will be frozen for a while and then unauthorized. Be sure to use this with care!
